<Page title="Bring the awkward case." description="Contribute to ArtemisKit through reproducible bug reports, documentation improvements, reviewed code or useful scenario ideas. Start with a small, specific contribution and the project’s current guidance. Keep examples sanitised, explain expected behaviour and include enough version and configuration detail for another person to investigate." eyebrow="Community & contributions"><h2>Where can I contribute?</h2><ul><li><strong>Bug reports:</strong> Include package versions, minimal inputs, expected behaviour and sanitised evidence.</li><li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Fix an unclear step, outdated command or missing limitation.</li><li><strong>Scenarios:</strong> Propose a real workflow with explicit success criteria and synthetic fixtures.</li><li><strong>Code:</strong> Discuss substantial changes in an issue before investing in an implementation.</li></ul><h2>Where should I start?</h2><div class="ak-actions"><a class="ak-btn" href="https://github.com/code-sensei/artemiskit/issues">Explore issues ↗</a><a class="ak-btn outline" href="https://github.com/code-sensei/artemiskit/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Contribution guide ↗</a></div><h2>Keep public reports safe to share</h2><p>Remove keys, personal data and proprietary material. Public GitHub issues are unsuitable for secrets or exploit details affecting live systems. Use the official Vorbtech website to establish an appropriate private reporting channel.</p><p><a href="https://www.vorbtech.com.ng/">Visit Vorbtech</a>.</p></Page>
